        <UserObject label="" link="# CLAUDE.mdProject context for Claude Code. Keep this file short and factual.## ProjectOrder management API for a small retail chain. Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Postgres.Deployed to Fly.io. Single repo, no monorepo tooling.## Commands- `make dev` — run the API locally on :8000 with hot reload- `make test` — full pytest suite (must pass before any commit)- `make test-unit` — fast subset, no DB required- `make lint` — ruff + mypy, both must be clean- `make migrate` — apply Alembic migrations- `make seed` — load fixture data into the local DB## Layout- `app/api/` — FastAPI routers, one module per resource- `app/services/` — business logic. Routers call services; services never import routers.- `app/models/` — SQLAlchemy models- `app/schemas/` — Pydantic request/response models- `tests/` — mirrors `app/` structure- `migrations/` — Alembic, autogenerated then hand-edited## Conventions- Line length 100, enforced by ruff. Don&#39;t reformat files you aren&#39;t otherwise touching.- Type hints on all function signatures. `mypy --strict` on `app/services/`.- No bare `except:`. Catch specific exceptions.- DB access only through `app/services/`. No queries in routers.- Tests use factories in `tests/factories.py`, not raw fixtures.- New endpoints need a test for the happy path and at least one failure case.## Gotchas- `app/legacy/` is dead code pending removal. Don&#39;t extend it, don&#39;t delete it yet.- The `orders.status` column is a plain string, not an enum, for historical reasons.  Validate against `OrderStatus` in `app/schemas/orders.py`.- Integration tests need a running Postgres. `make test` starts one via docker compose;  if Docker isn&#39;t running the suite fails with a confusing connection error.- Never commit to `main` directly. Branch, then PR.## Out of scopeDon&#39;t touch `infra/` or `.github/workflows/` unless asked explicitly." id="vuJTIm96bQAWBJX1B6yz-65">
          <mxCell parent="vuJTIm96bQAWBJX1B6yz-67" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="157.33" width="390" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
